{# The Chief of Staff's view of what the user has been doing (see
   src/tools/secretary/activity.py), rendered into the cached per-thread
   baseline: byte-deterministic for equal inputs, so no timestamps of its own,
   no dict iteration, and no guidance fence. How to use it is the role
   section's business; the lead-in only dates the copy. A user with nothing to
   list renders nothing rather than an empty element. #}
{% if content %}
<activity>
What the user has been doing, as of when this copy was frozen; a later activity row in the thread brings it up to date.

{{ content }}
</activity>
{% endif %}
